## Troubleshooting Flutter Device Connection Using AI

### Error Message
When I tried to run my Flutter application, my Android device was not detected.

```text
No supported devices connected.
```

### AI Suggested Steps
1. Check the USB cable connection.
2. Enable USB Debugging on the Android device.
3. Select File Transfer mode.
4. Allow the USB Debugging permission.
5. Run `flutter devices` to verify the connection.

### Solution
I reconnected my Android phone using a USB cable and enabled USB Debugging. After allowing the debugging permission, I ran `flutter devices` and my device was detected successfully.

### What Worked for Me
Enabling USB Debugging and reconnecting the USB cable solved my connection issue. After that, the `flutter run` command successfully launched my application on the physical device.